# THE DEV POD'S CARGO BOUND. One number, sourced rather than retyped.
#
#     set -a; . infra/dev/pod-build.env; set +a
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-11. Nothing in this repo bounds cargo's job count —
# there is no `.cargo/config.toml` — so cargo defaults to one job per
# CPU, which on this pod is 32, while the container's memory cgroup
# limit is 16 GiB. Concurrent builders took `memory.peak` to the full
# limit and the kernel killed seven background processes. Six keeps one
# builder inside its share when two or three are building at once.
#
# WHY NOT `.cargo/config.toml`: that file would bound the GATE and CI
# too. Both run one build at a time on a machine sized for it, and they
# are the authority that judges every car — slowing the judge to suit a
# shared dev box is the wrong trade. The bound belongs to the pod, so it
# lives in a file the pod's builders source and nothing else reads.
#
# Read by `boss brief` (which prints the line above, with this value in
# it) and by infra/dev/as-gate-uid.sh. Change the number here and both
# change; there is no second copy to keep in step.
CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6
